  "provenance": {
    "model_revision": "Hugging Face main of microsoft/Phi-3.5-mini-instruct read on 2026-11-03 (last modified 2025-12-10); passed to vllm serve as --revision, so the served weights are this commit",
    "why_overrides": "vLLM 0.11.0 Phi3LongRoPEScaledRotaryEmbedding.forward picks the short or long cos/sin table per forward pass with torch.any(positions > 4096) over the whole batch, so K/V cached under one table are read under the other (chunked prefill, decode past 4096, batch partners). The Phi run of 03/11/2026 failed gate G2 on this (LIHUA_ABLATION_PHI.md). The override makes RoPE static: the model's long_factor at every position, with the model's own attention scale.",
    "how": "--hf-overrides replaces rope_scaling (short_factor := long_factor) and the top-level original_max_position_embeddings (4096 -> 32768 = max_model_len). vLLM's llama.py copies the top-level value into rope_scaling, so the short/long switch never fires (positions < 32768) and the short table holds long_factor values. short_mscale = long_mscale = sqrt(1 + ln(131072/4096) / ln(4096)), the value vLLM and transformers derive from the unmodified config; passed explicitly because the derivation would otherwise use the overridden 32768.",
    "deviation": "Upstream Phi-3.5 applies short_factor to sequences of at most 4096 tokens. Here every sequence uses long_factor (as llama.cpp does when its context is above 4096). This is an intervention on the model's positional encoding and must be reported.",
    "pinned_config": "config.json of microsoft/Phi-3.5-mini-instruct at model_revision; its sha256 and both factor lists are in 'rope'",
    "vllm_version": "pinned in reproduce/modal_slm.py; slm_smoke.py reads GET /version to confirm",
    "served_alias": "third served model name, checked by slm_smoke.require_model, so the run refuses the unpatched Phi app (minirag-slm-phi)",
    "gpu": "A100-80GB as MiniCPM amendment M1: Phi keeps 32 K/V heads (0.375 MiB of KV a token); an A10G holds about one 32k window",
    "checked_at": "2026-11-07"
  }
